    "topic_path": "Early successes/Approaches/Reasoning, planning and problem solving as search/Heuristic Search",
    "content": "Many early AI programs used the same basic algorithm. To achieve some goal (like winning a game or proving a theorem), they proceeded step by step towards it (by making a move or a deduction) as if searching through a maze, backtracking whenever they reached a dead end.[97] The principal difficulty was that, for many problems, the number of possible paths through the maze was astronomical (a situation known as a combinatorial explosion). Researchers would reduce the search space by using heuristics that would eliminate paths that were unlikely to lead to a solution",
