    "topic_path": "Early successes/Optimism",
    "content": "The first generation of AI researchers made these predictions about their work: 1958, H. A. Simon and Allen Newell: \"within ten years a digital computer will be the world's chess champion\" and \"within ten years a digital computer will discover and prove an important new mathematical theorem.\"[127] 1965, H. A. Simon: \"machines will be capable, within twenty years, of doing any work a man can do.\"[128] 1967, Marvin Minsky: \"Within a generation... the problem of creating 'artificial intelligence' will substantially be solved.\"[129] 1970, Marvin Minsky (in Life magazine): \"In from three to eight years we will have a machine with the general intelligence of an average human being.\"[130][l]",
